Paper batch 1 of round 3: blocks U (refresh cells), N and Y judged and written into the paper

Stage runs/stage7_round3 (manifest, u/n/y.json) from analysis.round3_registered on the raw runs;
RThree macros and the generated tables tab_round3 and tab_reader; tests pin the staged verdicts and
values (tests/test_round3_paper.py).

Verdicts: U1 holds (R 1.00, 0.99 at D=1; 0.94, 0.92 at D_m), U2 reported, U3-U5 not judged (upsert
cells still running); N1 fails (S_src -4.5 pp [-17.5, +9.6], S_def +13.5 pp [+1.8, +25.3]); Y valid
(0 of 68,474 answers unreadable or cut off), Y1 and Y2 hold (+9.9, +5.3 pp on the other items), Y3
fails (Sonnet minus Qwen3.5-9B on definition items -8.7 and -15.2 pp).

Paper: the class split now names its reader wherever it is stated (abstract, introduction, results,
rules table, appendix C), and the abstract and introduction give the smaller but positive
definition-item interaction with Claude Sonnet 5.5 as reader; the Y3 gap is located at D=0 with
binding, where that reader re-derives the task filters from the records the stored statement quotes;
N1's verdict and reading are stated once in the results; the natural-branch placeholder is gone;
tab_round3 panel (c) drops the S_def row for the other items (n = 0) and says why in the caption; v4
and v4b join the registration tables. Main text ends on page 9.

